[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump weir with single concrete crest and brick walls and footbridge over structure. Previously station number 43801. GENERAL: Crump weir with single concrete crest and brick walls, 3.0m wide, with a footbridge over the structure. STATION HYDROMETRY: Bypassing is not significant, only at extremes. Weir seen to be drowned at 0.44m. One peak flow rating applied across the period of record. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Subject to stream support as part of an EA/Water Company operating agreement.
CATCHMENT,The catchment area consists of Upper Cretaceous (Upper and Middle Chalk), valley gravel and alluvium. No major urbanisation in the catchment. Land use rural and agricultural.
Qmed Suitability,Theoretical rating expected to perform well to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Theoretical rating does not account for drowned flows.
[END]
